    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d274">

                <pb facs="0446" n="1910" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p2/pg1910"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690D.91/12–451: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in India
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d274-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-04T18:11:00-05:00">December 4,
                            1951—6:11 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1113. Re Kashmir. Dept appreciates views expressed Embtel 1911 Nov 29. (Rptd
                    Karachi as 95, Paris Gadel as 37, London as 62). In event Graham has not
                    succeeded by Dec 22—due date his report<anchor n="2" xml:id="d274-f2"/>—we
                    believe if parties either tacitly or openly indicate a willingness for him
                    continue and SC does not specifically terminate his services he cld continue his
                    negots. Dept plans at working level confer immed future with UK re possible
                    courses action in event Graham’s present efforts unsuccessful.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d274-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d274-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Karachi as telegram 520, to Paris as Gadel 336, and to London as
                    2778.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d274-f2" n="2" xml:id="d274-f2-content">
                <p>The U.N. Representative for India and Pakistan transmitted his second report to
                    the Security Council on December 18, 1951 (U.N. document S/2448).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
